---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { repo, url, version } from "../lib/site";

const features = [
  {
    title: "JDKs from 20+ vendors",
    text: "Temurin, Corretto, Zulu, Liberica, Oracle, GraalVM, SapMachine, Semeru, Microsoft and more, from the foojay Disco API. Pick one per install or set a default, and keep GraalVM in its own GRAALVM_HOME slot for native-image.",
  },
  {
    title: "Maven, Gradle and sbt",
    text: "Straight from Maven Central, services.gradle.org and sbt's releases. Projects that use ./mvnw or ./gradlew keep their wrapper; jkit supplies the JDK.",
  },
  {
    title: "Per project",
    text: "jkit pin jdk@21 writes a jkit.toml, and jkit sync installs what it pins. It also reads the .sdkmanrc, .tool-versions or .java-version you already have. With auto-switch on, bash, zsh and fish follow it on cd.",
  },
  {
    title: "Per shell or globally",
    text: "jkit use jdk@21 changes this shell only; --global changes the default for every new terminal and app. jkit reset goes back.",
  },
  {
    title: "For CI, scripts and agents",
    text: "jkit exec jdk@17 -- mvn test runs one command with the right versions, no hook and no shell change. --json gives one document with a versioned schema, errors included.",
  },
  {
    title: "Says what it changed",
    text: "Every variable set, PATH entry added, link moved and file written is printed under the command's own message. Nothing changes quietly.",
  },
  {
    title: "Checked downloads",
    text: "HTTPS only, checked against the SHA-256 (or stronger) its source publishes before anything is unpacked. No checksum, no install, unless you ask for it. A failed install leaves nothing behind.",
  },
  {
    title: "status and doctor",
    text: "jkit status shows which version is active here and why. jkit doctor checks your setup and says how to fix each problem it finds.",
  },
  {
    title: "Native, no JDK needed",
    text: "A single binary built with GraalVM that starts in milliseconds. Linux and macOS on x64 and arm64, with signed and notarized macOS builds; Windows as a preview.",
  },
];
---

<Layout>
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="wrap hero-grid">
      <div>
        <p class="badge">v{version} · Linux, macOS and Windows (preview)</p>
        <h1>Install and switch JDKs, Maven, Gradle and sbt.</h1>
        <p class="lead">
          jkit is one small native command. Name a version, and an optional vendor, and it does
          the rest: per shell, per project or globally. No bash scripts, and no JDK needed to run it.
        </p>
        <p class="ctas">
          <a class="btn primary" href={url("install")}>Install jkit</a>
          <a class="btn" href={url("docs")}>Read the docs</a>
          <a class="btn" href={repo}>GitHub</a>
        </p>
      </div>
      <pre class="term" aria-label="Example terminal session"><span class="prompt">$ </span><span class="cmd">jkit install jdk@21</span>
<span class="dim">downloading jdk 21.0.13.1+2 temurin from github.com</span>
installed jdk 21.0.13.1+2 temurin → ~/.jkit/tools/jdk/21.0.13.1+2-temurin
<span class="dim">  link   ~/.jkit/global/jdk → ~/.jkit/tools/jdk/21.0.13.1+2-temurin</span>
<span class="prompt">$ </span><span class="cmd">jkit install jdk@17 zulu</span>
installed jdk 17.0.21.1+2 zulu → ~/.jkit/tools/jdk/17.0.21.1+2-zulu
<span class="prompt">$ </span><span class="cmd">jkit use jdk@17 zulu</span>
using jdk 17.0.21.1+2 zulu in this shell
<span class="dim">  set    JAVA_HOME=~/.jkit/tools/jdk/17.0.21.1+2-zulu
  PATH   + ~/.jkit/tools/jdk/17.0.21.1+2-zulu/bin</span>
<span class="prompt">$ </span><span class="cmd">java -version</span>
openjdk version "17.0.21.1" 2026-11-17 LTS</pre>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap">
    <h2>What it does</h2>
    <div class="grid">
      {features.map((f) => (
        <article class="card">
          <h3>{f.title}</h3>
          <p>{f.text}</p>
        </article>
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap">
    <h2>Versions that follow the project</h2>
    <p>
      Pin a version once and commit the <code>jkit.toml</code>. With the hook's auto-switch on,
      the shell switches when you <code>cd</code> into the project and back when you leave, and
      says each time what it changed.
    </p>
    <pre class="term"><span class="prompt">$ </span><span class="cmd">jkit pin jdk@21</span>
pinned jdk 21 in ~/src/app/jkit.toml
<span class="prompt">$ </span><span class="cmd">cd ~/src/app</span>
jkit: using ~/src/app/jkit.toml: jdk 21.0.13.1+2 temurin
<span class="dim">  set    JAVA_HOME=~/.jkit/tools/jdk/21.0.13.1+2-temurin
  PATH   + ~/.jkit/tools/jdk/21.0.13.1+2-temurin/bin</span>
<span class="prompt">$ </span><span class="cmd">cd ~</span>
jkit: left the project in ~/src/app: back to the global versions
<span class="dim">  set    JAVA_HOME=~/.jkit/global/jdk
  PATH   - ~/.jkit/tools/jdk/21.0.13.1+2-temurin/bin</span></pre>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap">
    <h2>Every major version, at a glance</h2>
    <p>
      <code>jkit search jdk</code> shows every vendor against every major version, with LTS
      releases marked and what you already have installed. <code>jkit search jdk@21</code> then
      lists each vendor's newest 21 build.
    </p>
    <pre class="term"><span class="prompt">$ </span><span class="cmd">jkit search jdk --maintained</span>
                  maintained
                  27 25 21 17 11 8 7
                     ‾‾ ‾‾ ‾‾ ‾‾ ‾ ‾
temurin *          ✓  ✓  ●  ✓  ✓ ✓
bisheng               ✓  ✓  ✓  ✓ ✓
corretto           ✓  ✓  ✓  ✓  ✓ ✓
dragonwell            ✓  ✓  ✓  ✓ ✓
eliya                 ✓
gluon-graalvm            ✓
graalvm               ✓  ✓  ✓
graalvm-ce            ✓  ✓  ✓
jetbrains             ✓  ✓  ✓  ✓
kona                  ✓  ✓  ✓  ✓ ✓
liberica           ✓  ✓  ✓  ✓  ✓ ✓
liberica-nik          ✓  ✓  ✓  ✓
mandrel               ✓  ✓  ✓  ✓
microsoft             ✓  ✓  ✓  ✓
openjdk            ✓  ✓  ✓  ✓  ✓ ✓
openlogic             ✓  ✓  ✓  ✓ ✓
oracle             ✓  ✓  ✓  ✓  ✓
sapmachine         ✓  ✓  ✓  ✓  ✓
semeru             ✓  ✓  ✓  ✓  ✓ ✓
semeru-certified      ✓  ✓  ✓  ✓
trava                          ✓ ✓
zulu               ✓  ✓  ✓  ●  ✓ ✓ ✓

<span class="dim">✓ available   ● installed   ‾‾ LTS   * default vendor
versions per vendor: jkit search jdk@&lt;major&gt;</span></pre>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap">
    <h2>Why not SDKMAN?</h2>
    <p>
      SDKMAN is great, but it is written in bash, so on Windows it needs WSL or Git Bash. jkit is a
      single native binary that runs in PowerShell too. It has its own command design: version
      prefixes like <code>jdk@21</code>, an optional vendor instead of IDs like
      <code>21.0.5-tem</code>, no interactive prompts, and a clear difference between this shell,
      the project and the global default. It reads <code>.sdkmanrc</code>, so a team can switch
      one person at a time.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap status">
    <h2>Status</h2>
    <p class="note">
      jkit {version} is the first public release. Linux and macOS are tested on every release;
      Windows works but is a preview: switching on <code>cd</code> and
      <code>jkit hook --install</code> aren't available in PowerShell yet. Also not yet: signature
      checks for more JDK vendors.
      Bugs and ideas are welcome in the <a href={`${repo}/issues`}>issue tracker</a>.
    </p>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .hero { background: var(--bg-soft); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); padding: 48px 0; }
  .hero-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 4fr 7fr; gap: 32px; align-items: center; }
  .hero .term { font-size: 0.72em; }
  .hero h1 { font-size: clamp(1.9rem, 4vw, 2.6rem); margin: 0.3em 0; }
  .lead { font-size: 1.15em; color: var(--muted); }
  .badge {
    display: inline-block; margin: 0; padding: 2px 10px; border-radius: 999px;
    background: var(--accent-soft); color: var(--accent); font-size: 0.85em; font-weight: 600;
  }
  .ctas { display: flex; gap: 10px; flex-wrap: wrap; margin-top: 1.5em; }
  .btn {
    display: inline-block; padding: 9px 16px; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid var(--border);
    color: var(--text); font-weight: 600; background: var(--bg);
  }
  .btn:hover { text-decoration: none; border-color: var(--accent); }
  .btn.primary { background: var(--accent); border-color: var(--accent); color: #fff; }
  .term { margin: 0; font-size: 0.85em; }
  .grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: 16px; }
  .card { border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 10px; padding: 4px 18px 8px; background: var(--bg); }
  .card h3 { font-size: 1.05em; margin-bottom: 0.3em; }
  .card p { color: var(--muted); margin-top: 0; }
  .status { padding-bottom: 48px; }
  @media (max-width: 860px) {
    .hero-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; }
  }
  @media (max-width: 560px) {
    .grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  }
</style>
